{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-05-Oct-2023-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Find the fourth proportional to 0.48, 0.84 and 32.", "options": [{"text": "65", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}, {"text": "56", "added": false}, {"text": "43", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The table shows data of population and literacy/illiteracy rate among the population in three different villages. The number of illiterates in village R is what percentage less than that in village P?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "In a circle of radius 42 cm, an arc subtends an angle of 60° at the centre. Find the length of the arc.", "options": [{"text": "44 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "21 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "22 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "42 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "Mihir buys a book for ₹625. However, because of certain urgency, he sells it for ₹550. Find his loss percentage.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The salary of Arpit fell by 5% after 1 year and further fell by 8% after the second year due to bad performance. Initially, his salary was ₹80,000. What is his current salary (in ₹)?", "options": [{"text": "69620", "added": false}, {"text": "69920", "added": false}, {"text": "70920", "added": false}, {"text": "65720", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The total surface area of a solid hemisphere is 4158 cm2. Find its volume (in cm3).", "options": [{"text": "462", "added": false}, {"text": "9702", "added": false}, {"text": "1848", "added": false}, {"text": "19404", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "The average weight of 8 students is 48 kg. If four students of average weight 44 kg and four students of average weight 58 kg is also added, then find the average weight of 16 students.", "options": [{"text": "49.5 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "48 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "49 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "48.5 kg", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "Simplify the given expression. (1 - 2x)2 - (1 + 2x)2", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1200", "added": false}, {"text": "800", "added": false}, {"text": "1000", "added": false}, {"text": "600", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "A boy goes from home to school at a speed of 30 km/h and returns back at a speed of 70 km/h. What is his average speed for the journey?", "options": [{"text": "42 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "48 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "38 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "36 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Rupu’s income is 20% more than Madhu’s income. Madhu’s income is less than Rupu’s income by:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "What annual instalment (in ₹) will discharge a debt of ₹9,429 due in three years at 12.25% simple interest per annum? [Note: Instalments will be paid at the end of Year 1, Year 2 and Year 3.]", "options": [{"text": "2,840", "added": false}, {"text": "2800", "added": false}, {"text": "2700", "added": false}, {"text": "2760", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-instalments", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The table shows the number of students studying in 6 different classes of 6 different schools. Which class has the minimum number of students from all schools together?", "options": [{"text": "VIII", "added": false}, {"text": "IX", "added": false}, {"text": "VII", "added": false}, {"text": "X", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "Find the least number which is exactly divisible by 20, 28, 34, 60 and 75.", "options": [{"text": "36220", "added": false}, {"text": "35900", "added": false}, {"text": "34500", "added": false}, {"text": "35700", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "The mean proportional between 0.03 and 0.0003 is:", "options": [{"text": "0.0003", "added": false}, {"text": "0.0013", "added": false}, {"text": "0.003", "added": false}, {"text": "0.033", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "108°", "added": false}, {"text": "105°", "added": false}, {"text": "100°", "added": false}, {"text": "90°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "A shopkeeper increases the cost price of an item by 50% and offers a discount of 40% on this marked price. What is his loss percentage?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "An item with a marked price of ₹z was sold for ₹6,622, after a discount of 12% was offered. What was the value of z?", "options": [{"text": "₹7,425", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,525", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,575", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "Study the given bar graph carefully to answer the question that follows. Marks obtained by four students in Mid-I and Mid-II. Marks obtain by Hemanth in Mid-I are what percentage of the total marks obtained by all the students in Mid-I?", "options": [{"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "The following table shows the income of a company in a year from various sectors: What is the difference (in lakh ₹) between the income from the maximum earning sector and the minimum earning sector?", "options": [{"text": "48", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "55", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "If interest be compounded half-yearly, then find the compound interest on ₹8,000 at 20% p.a. for 1 year.", "options": [{"text": "₹1,675", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,690", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,685", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,680", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "33", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "If 2 men or 4 women can build a wall in 34 days, in how many days can 6 men and 5 women build the same wall?", "options": [{"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "efficiency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "Find the HCF of 78, 84, 90 and 112.", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹40,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹55,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹50,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹45,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "Mahesh agreed to sell rice with 24% loss, as the rice got rotten. However, he cheated customers and gave only 19 gm of rice in place of 50 gm of rice. What is the percentage of his profit or loss?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "A cylinder has some water in it at a height of 16 cm. If a sphere of radius 9 cm is put into it, then find the rise in the height of the water if the radius of the cylinder is 12 cm.", "options": [{"text": "8 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "6 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8.75 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "6.75 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "If the radius of two circles be 6 cm and 9 cm and the length of the transverse common tangent be 20 cm, then find the distance between the two centres.", "options": [{"text": "25 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "22 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "24 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "27 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "Nikunj goes 4 kilometres against the current of a stream in 1 hour, and 2 kilometres along the current in 15 minutes. How long will it take him to go 7 kilometres in stationary water?", "options": [{"text": "1 hour 15 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "1 hour 20 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "1 hour 10 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "1 hour 5 minutes", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "upstream-downstream", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "At 7: 30 P.M. the owner of a Cycle noticed that a thief is taking away his cycle from his home and is cycling in a particular direction at an estimated speed of 10 km per hour. He informed the police about the theft and the policeman started from the same point, half an hour later than the time of the theft but with a speed of 12 km per hour. At what time will Policeman catch the thief?", "options": [{"text": "10:45 P.M.", "added": false}, {"text": "9: 30 P.M.", "added": false}, {"text": "10:00 P.M.", "added": false}, {"text": "10:30 P.M.", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "early-late", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹18,75,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹26,80,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹24,75,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹21,55,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "In a ∆ABC, the bisectors of angle ABC and angle ACB intersect each other at point O. If the angle BOC is 125°, then the angle BAC is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "75°", "added": false}, {"text": "78°", "added": false}, {"text": "70°", "added": false}, {"text": "82°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "Two trains Mumbai Rajdhani and Kissan Express of lengths 850 m and 700 m are 1050 m apart, and are running on parallel tracks towards each other. Mumbai Rajdhani is running at 62 km/h and Kissan Express is running at 55 km/h. In how much time (in sec) will the trains cross each other?", "options": [{"text": "70", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "75", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1150 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "780 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "1083 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "960 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "frustum-prism-pyramid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "The sides of a rectangle are in the ratio of 3 : 8 and its area is 1944 cm2. What is its perimeter?", "options": [{"text": "189 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "208 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "198 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "308 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "A and B complete a work in 24 and 30 days, respectively, working 10 hours per day. The work is to be done in two shifts. The morning shift is for 6 hours and the evening shift is for 4 hours. On the first day, A works in the morning and B works in the evening, and they interchange their shifts every day. On which day did the work get completed?", "options": [{"text": "21st day", "added": false}, {"text": "24th day", "added": false}, {"text": "30th day", "added": false}, {"text": "27th day", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 43, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 44, "text": "The height and the radius of the base of a right circular cone are in the ratio of 12 : 5. If its volume is 314 cm3, then what is the slant height of the cone? (Use π = 3.14)", "options": [{"text": "12 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "11 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "13 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "14 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 45, "text": "Three numbers are in the ratio of 5 : 7 : 9 and their LCM is 34,650. Their HCF is:", "options": [{"text": "315", "added": false}, {"text": "55", "added": false}, {"text": "110", "added": false}, {"text": "99", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 46, "text": "Which is the largest number that divides each of 1036, 1813 and 3885 without leaving any remainder?", "options": [{"text": "333", "added": false}, {"text": "111", "added": false}, {"text": "259", "added": false}, {"text": "37", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 47, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 48, "text": "In an election between two candidates, 20% of the voters on the voters list did not cast their votes and 80 voters cast their ballot papers blank. The winner secured 45% of all the voters in the list and he got 280 votes more than his rival. The number of voters on the list was:", "options": [{"text": "1500", "added": false}, {"text": "2800", "added": false}, {"text": "2500", "added": false}, {"text": "2000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 49, "text": "Find the LCM of 73 and 657.", "options": [{"text": "73", "added": false}, {"text": "657", "added": false}, {"text": "146", "added": false}, {"text": "365", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 50, "text": "In a circle, chords AB and CD intersect internally at E. If CD = 18 cm, DE = 5cm, AE = 13 cm, then the length of BE is:", "options": [{"text": "4 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "7 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "3 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "5 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}]}